{"data": [{"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-28T21:32:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115557327663235434"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Suppliers are passing homes received from developers to their own creditors, settling bills without cash but facing valuation and title-transfer risks", "display_url": "caixinglobal.com/2026-10-26/pro…", "end": 266, "expanded_url": "https://www.caixinglobal.com/2026-10-26/properties-pass-down-chinas-construction-supply-chain-in-a-debt-relay-102497611.html", "images": [{"height": 373, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115557332897693696/Pq3v945L?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 560}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115557332897693696/Pq3v945L?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 243, "status": 200, "title": "Properties Pass Down China’s Construction Supply Chain in a ‘Debt Relay’", "unwound_url": "https://www.caixinglobal.com/2026-10-26/properties-pass-down-chinas-construction-supply-chain-in-a-debt-relay-102497611.html", "url": "https://t.co/PTRDFMs11U"}]}, "id": "2115557327663235434", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 669, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "\"Chinese construction suppliers are using homes received against unpaid bills to repay their own creditors—sometimes before taking legal ownership—as the property downturn strains payments across the industry, recent company disclosures show\"\nhttps://t.co/PTRDFMs11U", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2115557327663235434"}, {"author_id": "48463418", "created_at": "2026-10-28T21:19:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115553972119331307"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "We investigate the conditions under which black hole fragmentation, the splitting of a black hole into two or multiple smaller ones, may occur via an unspecified dynamics, which would have the topology of a pair-of-pants. We employ kinematical and entropical consideration on time-sliced quasistatic black hole configurations to check under what conditions the pants dynamics is permitted. In classical general relativity, the Bekenstein-Hawking area law forbids such processes for Schwarzschild black holes. For spinning Kerr black holes, purely kinematic analyses impose constraints that prevent fragmentation, even in regimes where entropy considerations might allow it, except possibly in near-extremal cases. We then hunt for scenarios where black holes can wear pants: from the well-known Gregory-Laflamme instability in higher dimensions, to the potential effect of superradiant instabilities in nonaxisymmetric radiation trapping, to finally gravitational models that modify the relations bet", "display_url": "go.aps.org/4z0rtWy", "end": 206, "expanded_url": "https://go.aps.org/4z0rtWy", "start": 183, "status": 200, "title": "When black holes admit pair-of-pants topologies", "unwound_url": "https://journals.aps.org/prd/abstract/10.1103/cx69-t466", "url": "https://t.co/aVzGIH99Co"}]}, "id": "2115553972119331307", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 278, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Black holes can merge, but can they split? A study in Physical Review D explores when a black hole could break apart into a \"pair of pants\" shape, and when it can't.\n\nRead the study: https://t.co/aVzGIH99Co", "url": "https://x.com/APSphysics/status/2115553972119331307"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-28T21:08:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115551366290550877"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 6, "id": "239026022", "start": 0, "username": "SamRo"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/ZRnab1FYCA", "end": 44, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115551366290550877/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115551358392659968", "start": 21, "url": "https://t.co/ZRnab1FYCA"}]}, "id": "2115551366290550877", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 8097, "like_count": 42, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@SamRo this is elite https://t.co/ZRnab1FYCA", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115551366290550877"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-28T20:58:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115548849154744737"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/arkdavey/statu…", "end": 288, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/arkdavey/status/2100584566868074624", "start": 265, "url": "https://t.co/CJnBp4wRvv"}]}, "id": "2115548849154744737", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 7603, "like_count": 11, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2100584566868074624", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "“accessibility\" is the side they want to be on &amp; closes off critique in academia.”\n\nI heard a local community organizer (who’s gotten involved with the efforts to save the Tompkins bars) say almost the exact same thing with respect to local government debates. https://t.co/CJnBp4wRvv", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115548849154744737"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-28T20:38:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115543673211617556"], "id": "2115543673211617556", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 10931, "like_count": 140, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 10}, "text": "AI is creating so much volatility right now, which you can see everywhere except in the volatility statistics.", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115543673211617556"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-10-28T20:36:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115543312417595606"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/KGeorgieva/sta…", "end": 191, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/KGeorgieva/status/2115518197004918834", "start": 168, "url": "https://t.co/mlI0b7Sx8X"}]}, "id": "2115543312417595606", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1018, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115518197004918834", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "interesting move for Liao Min, probably means his career has plateaued in the PRC system, wonder if they replace him with someone harder line for US-China negotiations https://t.co/mlI0b7Sx8X", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2115543312417595606"}, {"author_id": "30034124", "created_at": "2026-10-28T20:16:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115538098557751521"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 32, "id": "3433145842", "start": 20, "username": "LBNFacility"}, {"end": 106, "id": "3906355332", "start": 94, "username": "DUNEScience"}], "urls": [{"description": "Construction of the Long-Baseline Neutrino Facility is entering its next phase, marking a major step forward for the international Deep Underground Neutrino Experiment hosted by Fermilab. With the arrival of critical components and growing momentum across partner institutions, DUNE is moving closer to unlocking long standing mysteries in particle physics and the origins of the universe.", "display_url": "news.fnal.gov/2026/10/moment…", "end": 131, "expanded_url": "https://news.fnal.gov/2026/10/momentum-builds-for-world-leading-neutrino-experiment-hosted-by-fermilab/", "images": [{"height": 900, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115538104337481728/63TqMvBs?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115538104337481728/63TqMvBs?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 108, "status": 200, "title": "Momentum builds for world-leading neutrino experiment hosted by Fermilab", "unwound_url": "https://news.fnal.gov/2026/10/momentum-builds-for-world-leading-neutrino-experiment-hosted-by-fermilab/", "url": "https://t.co/ihnp9BLuaG"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/YlJJ6CpvWU", "end": 155, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Fermilab/status/2115538098557751521/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115538095739138048", "start": 132, "url": "https://t.co/YlJJ6CpvWU"}]}, "id": "2115538098557751521", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 626, "like_count": 20, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Construction of the @LBNFacility is entering its next phase, marking a major step forward for @DUNEScience.\nhttps://t.co/ihnp9BLuaG https://t.co/YlJJ6CpvWU", "url": "https://x.com/Fermilab/status/2115538098557751521"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-10-28T19:59:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115533944448049454"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/BB1f0M7UJf", "end": 62, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2115533944448049454/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115533893948383232", "start": 39, "url": "https://t.co/BB1f0M7UJf"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/BB1f0M7UJf", "end": 62, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2115533944448049454/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115533893952528384", "start": 39, "url": "https://t.co/BB1f0M7UJf"}, {"display_url": "x.com/niubi/status/2…", "end": 86, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/niubi/status/2115530994551758868", "start": 63, "url": "https://t.co/lxhDyswNia"}]}, "id": "2115533944448049454", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 3014, "like_count": 15, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115530994551758868", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "what a coincidence...and it is working https://t.co/BB1f0M7UJf https://t.co/lxhDyswNia", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2115533944448049454"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-10-28T19:47:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115530994551758868"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "State-funded tours, co-ordinated hashtags, cash competitions... Beijing counters criticism of its new Ethnic Unity Law via foreigners on social media.", "display_url": "toosimple.substack.com/p/how-china-is…", "end": 83, "expanded_url": "https://toosimple.substack.com/p/how-china-is-covertly-using-western?r=2e&utm_campaign=post-expanded-share&utm_medium=web", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115530995193577473/OfyfqChe?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1600}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115530995193577473/OfyfqChe?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 60, "status": 200, "title": "How China is covertly using Western influencers in Xinjiang", "unwound_url": "https://toosimple.substack.com/p/how-china-is-covertly-using-western?r=2e&utm_campaign=post-expanded-share&utm_medium=web", "url": "https://t.co/NRRvU0C7Q2"}]}, "id": "2115530994551758868", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 3558, "like_count": 15, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "How China is covertly using Western influencers in Xinjiang https://t.co/NRRvU0C7Q2 \"the foreign influencers and the Chinese state are playing a dangerous game. And the hashtags establish a direct link between supposed ‘individual accounts’ and Chinese state propaganda campaigns.", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2115530994551758868"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-28T19:43:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115529809031991449"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/HGb0ezjtlP", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2115529809031991449/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115529805848526848", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/HGb0ezjtlP"}]}, "id": "2115529809031991449", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1216, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Q1 Business Employment Dynamics:\n\n1/ The labor market is \"frozen\", with lower hiring &amp; separations relative to pre-pandemic.\n\nBUT: turnover due to \"creative destruction\" (openings/births &amp; closings/deaths of establishments) has actually increased over this same period. https://t.co/HGb0ezjtlP", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2115529809031991449"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-10-28T19:35:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115527811259912230"], "id": "2115527811259912230", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 2364, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "who from dc think tanks/universities is going to this? \"Against this backdrop, the “China-US Intergenerational Dialogue 2026,” jointly hosted by The Paper and the Shanghai Institutes for International Studies, will be held in Shanghai on October 30. The event’s Chinese theme is", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2115527811259912230"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-28T19:24:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115525147323248744"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 128, "id": "33805522", "start": 115, "username": "sunraysunray"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/P3jDV3UV0t", "end": 283, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115525147323248744/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115525014506065920", "start": 260, "url": "https://t.co/P3jDV3UV0t"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/P3jDV3UV0t", "end": 283, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115525147323248744/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115525033137225728", "start": 260, "url": "https://t.co/P3jDV3UV0t"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/P3jDV3UV0t", "end": 283, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115525147323248744/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115525056172322816", "start": 260, "url": "https://t.co/P3jDV3UV0t"}, {"display_url": "x.com/analytichegel/…", "end": 307, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/analytichegel/status/2115473662363271560", "start": 284, "url": "https://t.co/OUyMFzh9zN"}]}, "id": "2115525147323248744", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 83, "impression_count": 18113, "like_count": 125, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 18, "retweet_count": 16}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115473662363271560", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "WILL AI MAKE CAPITALISM OBSOLETE?\n\nIn today's newsletter, I wrote about a brief moment at the end of our chat with @sunraysunray (actually it was kind of after the end of the episode, but our producers left it in, which is good) about AI and central planning. https://t.co/P3jDV3UV0t https://t.co/OUyMFzh9zN", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115525147323248744"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-28T19:16:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115523039354073451"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/pVAmxgNzsK", "end": 295, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115523039354073451/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115521630130573312", "start": 272, "url": "https://t.co/pVAmxgNzsK"}]}, "id": "2115523039354073451", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12125, "like_count": 51, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "City Council Member Harvey Epstein and State Assembly Member Keith Powers have come out in favor of preserving the existing exercise equipment at Tompkins Square. I still think this ADA angle is a bit of a red herring, designed to make the bars defenders look like jerks. https://t.co/pVAmxgNzsK", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115523039354073451"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-10-28T19:09:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115521396331991380"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "China's proposed artificial intelligence export curbs will push a business model favoured by Beijing and the industry's biggest players: keeping ​valuable technology at home while selling access to it abroad as rivalry with the US intensifies.", "display_url": "reuters.com/business/retai…", "end": 87, "expanded_url": "https://www.reuters.com/business/retail-consumer/chinas-new-export-curbs-draw-line-around-its-ai-crown-jewels-2026-10-28/", "images": [{"height": 1005, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115357406821490688/Gq9QJBb_?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115357406821490688/Gq9QJBb_?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 64, "status": 200, "title": "China's new export curbs draw a line around its AI crown jewels", "unwound_url": "https://www.reuters.com/business/retail-consumer/chinas-new-export-curbs-draw-line-around-its-ai-crown-jewels-2026-10-28/", "url": "https://t.co/IuFfgitCdd"}]}, "id": "2115521396331991380", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1195, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "China's new export curbs draw a line around its AI crown jewels https://t.co/IuFfgitCdd \"Researchers at major Chinese AI labs are seeking clarification on whether they can train or run their most advanced models on foreign-owned overseas servers, according to a person briefed on", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2115521396331991380"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-28T19:07:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115520963378917876"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 19, "start": 14, "tag": "ORCL"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/lGeSYpFOlc", "end": 83, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115520963378917876/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115520945972449280", "start": 60, "url": "https://t.co/lGeSYpFOlc"}]}, "id": "2115520963378917876", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 9608, "like_count": 49, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "Nice rally in $ORCL 10-year bonds, with a strong move today https://t.co/lGeSYpFOlc", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115520963378917876"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-28T19:00:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115519042354053475"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 35, "id": "2356714968", "start": 22, "username": "HyunSongShin"}]}, "id": "2115519042354053475", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 9023, "like_count": 17, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Warsh just called out @HyunSongShin and said he's talented and he's glad to see him managing the central bank of Korea", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115519042354053475"}, {"author_id": "961132338", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:56:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115518065823945194"], "id": "2115518065823945194", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2255, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Seems as if he is trying to put us to sleep", "url": "https://x.com/M_C_Klein/status/2115518065823945194"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:54:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115517527795372515"], "id": "2115517527795372515", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1214, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "\"As the economy slumped in recent yrs, the strain on Chinese companies has increased &amp; their finances have deteriorated. Total net profit at 5,400 🇨🇳 companies listed on local stock exchanges fell for the 3rd consecutive yr in 2025...Excess factory capacity &amp; weak domestic demand", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2115517527795372515"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:53:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115517408203116887"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Explore the most interesting topics in finance, markets and economics, for subscribers only.", "display_url": "bloomberg.com/account/newsle…", "end": 155, "expanded_url": "https://www.bloomberg.com/account/newsletters/odd-lots", "images": [{"height": 675, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113338194108219392/GXbIwo9k?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113338194108219392/GXbIwo9k?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 132, "status": 200, "title": "Odd Lots", "unwound_url": "https://www.bloomberg.com/account/newsletters/odd-lots", "url": "https://t.co/25c7dc92bu"}]}, "id": "2115517408203116887", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 11909, "like_count": 81, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "\"I'm not a Wall Street newsletter\" -- Kevin Warsh\n\nNeither am I, but I do co-write a newsletter which you should subscribe to here. https://t.co/25c7dc92bu", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115517408203116887"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:49:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115516249031803280"], "id": "2115516249031803280", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 11034, "like_count": 98, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 19, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "FOMC press conferences don't have a long history, so as I've said before, I don't think it'd be the end of the world if they got rid of them. \n\nAnd actually, given how little Warsh says during these pressers, it's surprising he hasn't killed them yet.", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115516249031803280"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:45:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115515400377249900"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 259, "id": "793097212070944768", "start": 248, "username": "IraFJersey"}]}, "id": "2115515400377249900", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 10580, "like_count": 48, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "Warsh noted that there will be few policy setting meetings going forward, suggesting that some meetings may price for greater moves and risks and more rate-market volatility around meetings, particularly if forward guidance continues to be reduced\n@IraFJersey", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2115515400377249900"}, {"author_id": "961132338", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:45:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115515302683591162"], "id": "2115515302683591162", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1541, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "If the one strategy meeting in 2027 goes reasonably well, why would the Fed need to have *two* strategy meetings in 2028?", "url": "https://x.com/M_C_Klein/status/2115515302683591162"}, {"author_id": "2961589380", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:43:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115514869155868878"], "id": "2115514869155868878", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 10300, "like_count": 52, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "Fed is shifting to a 7/1 then 6/2 meeting schedule: 7 on policy, 1 on major economic issues in 2027; followed by 6 and 2 in 2028", "url": "https://x.com/LizAnnSonders/status/2115514869155868878"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:37:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115513407327944829"], "id": "2115513407327944829", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 8969, "like_count": 29, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "*WARSH: FOMC SCHEDULE WILL CHANGE AS OF NEXT FALL", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115513407327944829"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-28T18:37:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115513263060406502"], "id": "2115513263060406502", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 19296, "like_count": 61, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "*ORACLE TO LIMIT ADDITIONAL CAPITAL RAISES TO $20B FOR FY27-FY30", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2115513263060406502"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "497231011", "name": "China Beige Book", "username": "ChinaBeigeBook"}, {"id": "48463418", "name": "American Physical Society", "